Yes, that's why you wear a amulet of life saving.  Of course, seven
amulets of life saving weren't enough to save my 30th level Valkyrie. 
Sit back and hear a tale of woe fit for the bards...

I had the bell, book and candleabra, but I didn't have any candles. 
There were only three candles in the light store in the mines, so I had
to scrounge some more.  I tried polypiling them repeatedly, but I only
managed to scrounge two more through this and I was rapidly running out
of tools.  Since at this point I hadn't yet won 3.1, I was determined to
finish it.  I had taken to wandering around, just praying for a wand of
polymorph or a candle.  Then came the biggest run of bad luck I have
ever had the mispleasure of witnessing (not to mention a healthy dose of
pure stupidity).

I was wandering through the quest area when I waltzed into some lava
while standing next to some fire ants.  My boots of speed caught on
fire.  "Damn!" I think.  Since I was angry, I wasn't thinking too
clearly, and I decided to take it out on the ants instead of getting out
of the lava.  Dumb move.  Glub glub glub.  Death number 1.  I get out,
leave the quest area and find a lamp.  Since I have plenty of holy
water, I bless it on the off chance it is magic, and I start rubbing it.
 It isn't magic.  Sigh.  So, I go wandering off again, forgetting to
wield Vorpal Blade.  Boom, I'm surrounded by four dragons, a couple of
umber hulks and a cockatrice.  I also faint from hunger (duh).  Stoned. 
Death number 2.  I wake up, first action is to put on another life
saving amulet.  Second is to pray.  No dice, my god is displeased,
probably since I've got food in the bag but was afraid I'd faint again
before I'd get a chance to eat it.  Nighty night.  Stoned again.  Death
number 3.  I wake up, put on another amulet, get some food from the bag
and do manage a munch.  Okay, I've lost a few amulets, but no big deal. 
I kill the cockatrice and then decide to start in on the dragons.  At
this point, a gremlin wanders up and there is, of course, a pool in the
room.  Did I mention that it was at this point that the Wizard of Yendor
decides to show up?  How about that nymph over yonder?  Don't blink,
here is where it really starts moving fast.  Also don't forget that I'm
stil wielding a lamp...

I teleport to a corner so I can only get attacked by three monsters at
the same time.  I choose the corner away from the dragons, since I
figure the gremlins won't do much to me since I they don't live long
near me.  Miscalculation:  I forgot I was using a lamp and I forgot I
lost my speed boots.  First round, one gremlin chuckles.  Of course, the
little bastard stole my intrisic speed.  Wonderful.  The nymph decides
to swipe my shield of reflection.  Wonderful.  The Wizard moves and
tries the finger of death.  Phew, I've still got my GDSM.  I pound a
gremlin, but don't kill it since I've still got a lamp for a weapon. 
This round, the dirtbag gremlins steals sleep resistance.  Aargh!  I
thump the same gremlin and when it doesn't kill him, I figure something
is wrong here.  The wizard pounds me, I 'port, he follows.  I walk onto
the trap in the corner since I know it is a sleep trap, corners are
defensible, I couldn't 'port directly there, and I've got sleep
resistance so why worry?  Er.  Nighty, night.  Wizard does double
trouble, then summons pets three times.  I get hashed in a big, big way.
 I wake up, wield Vorpal Blade.  Get hashed.  My finger slips and I try
to attack the gelatinous cube.  Paralysis.  Toast.  Death number 4.  I
decide enough is enough, invoke the Orb of Fate, and head down to the
Valley of the Dead.  The two wizards follow, summon pets again.  One of
them, of course, has a wand of death.  Of course, my shield of
reflection had been stolen.  "Send in the clones..."  Death number 5. 
I'm mad.  Really mad.  I lop lots of heads off.  Things are going great
again.  That is, until the marilith with Stormbringer comes after me. 
Stormbringer!  That hurt, alot.  Also, I didn't know which of the three
or so had it.  I guessed wrong.  This, along with a couple of wizards
and pets, meant, that's right, Death number 6.  Things are getting grim.
 I only have one amulet left.  I kill the bastard with Strombringer and
stand on it so nobody else can use.  The next death isn't that
great...it mainly involves me trying to fight off tons and tons of
dragons.  Did I mention that I still had _no_ speed and also lost my
blessing of armor class earlier (and my +5 shield of reflection)?  Death
number 7.  I'm out of amulets.  I'm running low on hit points, but I've
almost eliminated the hoard.  If I can just get healed...# pray.

